'm just  you know trying to go and take as many  good at-bats I can and  and get on base as much as I can  especially with Bellinger hitting behind  me I feel like I'm in scoring position  if I can just get to first base so you  know it's a cool thing obviously  everything is going good but we still  got a lot of baseball left and to start  looking at it now I think would be doing  myself a disservice there a part of you  that wishes the playoffs started right  now aside from not having Kershaw there  but the way you guys have been playing  yeah you know even asked that a lot I  think you know with as many veterans as  we have we do have a lot of young guys  still and there's still room for  everyone to grow not just young guys I  think everyone can learn and get better  and try to figure out what we're trying  to do here and the amount of information  that this game has to offer now is crazy  and I think we're kind of on the on the  brink of grasping it and how to turn  numbers into information that you can  actually use on the field and our  coaching staff has been unbelievable so  I think you know this last you know  month or so we're going to take the time  and take advantage of trying to get  better with all the information we have  and how we can put it to use and how we  can how we can make it help us win games  on a field in the class he's Justin  Turner he's leading the National League  he was an all-star leading the National  League and hitting what explained to me  after right before that 2014 season it's  a pretty amazing story though when you  consider you you were let go by the Mets  and then you're just sort of floating  out there and then you end up with the  Dodgers like how do you how do you put  all that together if you were trying to  explain it to somebody yeah that was a  that was a tough time for me I was  actually heading down to the Players  Association meetings in San Diego as of  representative for the Mets and on my  way down I got the phone call from sandy  saying that they needed some roster  space and they wish they were you know  letting me go and non-tender me and you  know that offseason was hard I would get  calls from my agent every other day  saying oh this seems interested this  thing  interested and then nothing would come  of it and you know you hear a team name  and you get excited and you start you  know looking at their roster and their  stuff and then the next day that team's  out of it and it was a brutal process  and at the end it came down to it  actually came down to the Red Sox and  twins and I was getting close to make a  decision and Marlon Byrd called me and  he was good friends with Michael Young  who was with the Dodgers at the time and  he was trying to make a decision on  whether he was going to come back and  play one more year or whether he was  going to retire so Marlon called me and  said hey don't sign anywhere yet if  Michael Young decides to retire  I think the Dodgers are going to call  you oh man and sure enough I think a  couple days later Michael decided he  want to spend time with the family and  then my phone rang and and the doctor  called if I would have told you at that  time when the Dodgers called a by the  way you're going to start and you're  going to lead the National League in  hitting one year yeah that'd have been  hard too hard to see at that time I was  going through some stuff making some  changes in my swing and trying to get  better but that that definitely would  have it hard to see how good were used a  little leaguer I think I was a good  player I don't think I was a standout  guy I was always small in my junior high  school I was only five nine hundred  thirty pounds so I never really stuck  out on the field I had to take advantage  of trying to be as smart as I could and  be a baseball player to get noticed and  then eventually you know through college  and when I got pro ball I started being  a little bit bigger and stronger and and  the ball started going a little further  for me I love the story about ed sheeran  who was at Staples in any warrior Jersey  out for an encore there this just feels  like ginger on ginger love there okay  right is that what you you see with that  cheer yeah that was crazy I actually had  no idea he was doing that we were trying  to reach out to him cuz we knew it was  in LA we knew we were in LA we were  trying to get him to come to the stadium  come to a game or at least come in the  clubhouse and  and talked to some guys and it didn't  end up working out and then next thing I  know you know we get in the locker room  from the game and my phone has a million  messages on it saying the edge here is  wearing your Jersey for the Encore  playing shape of you right now at the  Staples Center I'm like what and then I  get all these videos and pictures and  text and yeah it was pretty crazy and  they did begin the next night so  definitely feel pretty honored about  that and hopefully I'll get to go see  them in concert one day make is this  your walk-up song yeah when did you tell  your song from day one this year I've  been using it so I heard of the thought  season liked it obviously he's a ginger  so I was like this is it this is this is  what we're going with this here so it  couldn't worked out any better yeah but  you strike me a little more hardcore  music than than Ed Sheeran I kid I do  you like metal you know rock and roll  I like everything I don't love metal but  I'll listen to a Brandon McCarthy when  he works out play some pretty heavy  stuff and yeah I'm probably the only guy  on the team that doesn't mind it but I  like everything I don't I don't  discriminate I if as long as there's a  beat to it I'll listen to it all I  played music all the time in the  clubhouse and four guys and I try to  cover all the genres and keep everyone  happy so yeah well that's why you're the  team leader hey yeah I guess Hey  Congrats on the success so far and  certainly a grea